{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q325345","formula":"CuS","hill":"CuS","elements":["S","Cu"],"composition":{"S":1.0,"Cu":1.0},"names":{"en":"Covellite","ru":"Ковеллин","uk":"Ковелін"},"descriptions":{"en":"Covellite (also known as covelline) is a rare copper sulfide mineral with the formula CuS. This indigo blue mineral is commonly a secondary mineral in limited abundance and although it is not an important ore of copper itself, it is well known to mineral collectors. The mineral is generally found in zones of secondary enrichment (supergene) of copper sulfide deposits. Commonly found as coatings on chalcocite, chalcopyrite, bornite, enargite, pyrite, and other sulfides, it often occurs as pseudomorphic replacements of other minerals.","ru":"Ковелли́н (или ковеллит) — минерал, сульфид меди. Название получил в честь итальянского геолога и исследователя Н. Ковелли (1790—1829), который в начале XIX века обнаружил новый минерал в окрестностях вулкана Везувия.","uk":"Ковелі́н, або мі́дне інди́го, або ковелі́т (рос. ковеллин; англ. covellite, covelline, covellinite, indigo copper; нім."},"fame":37,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-504","atoms":24,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[3.768,0.0,0.0],[-1.884,3.263,0.0],[0.0,0.0,16.327]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":0.0,"y":2.175,"z":6.427,"el":"Cu"},{"x":1.884,"y":1.088,"z":14.59,"el":"Cu"},{"x":1.884,"y":1.088,"z":9.9,"el":"Cu"},{"x":0.0,"y":2.175,"z":1.736,"el":"Cu"},{"x":1.884,"y":1.088,"z":4.082,"el":"Cu"},{"x":0.0,"y":2.175,"z":12.245,"el":"Cu"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":7.116,"el":"S"},{"x":-1.884,"y":3.263,"z":7.116,"el":"S"},{"x":3.768,"y":0.0,"z":7.116,"el":"S"},{"x":1.884,"y":3.263,"z":7.116,"el":"S"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":15.28,"el":"S"},{"x":-1.884